- **Evidence:** runs/2026-11-01_PHI@WSH/checklist.md Phase 14 row.

## BUG-2026-11-01-BIAS — bias model hard-coded flat haircuts (FIXED in tools/sim_v6.py, 2026-11-01; Nov 1 runs still on v5)
- Found: Ghost6 vet 07:40 ET; confirmed by Blitz 07:36–07:45 ET.
- Root cause: runs/2026-11-01_shared_src/sim_v5.py line 65 `vf,cf,yf=(0.92,0.97,0.95) if mode=='bias'` — flat volume/catch/yards cuts not calibrated to results.
- Evidence (199 Nov 1 legs, median minus line, mean %): bias -16.3% (passyds -17.7, rec -16.9, recyds -20.5, rushrec -14.6, rushyds -4.9); MC -1.9%; GR -5.8%. Avg(p) edge on unders +13.3 pts vs overs +6.4 pts; MC alone is symmetric (+9.8 vs +10.9). 127/199 candidates and 15/19 passes were unders.
- Today's handling: edge decision uses avg(MC, GR); bias p/median still recorded and the gate (unchanged) still requires every model p>=.45 and median clearing the line. Note added to every Nov 1 manifest (edge_decision) and report Risks.
- Fix plan (not done, not in time for today): tools/sim_v6.py with bias-mode factors calibrated on model-vs-actual residuals by market (nflverse 2026 weekly + postmortems), test-first (median residual ~0 per market). sim_v5.py is in runs/ shared_src, not nfl-sim/.
- Root cause, confirmed by backtest: (1) v5 line 65 applies a flat vol .92 x catch .97 x yds .95 cut. That is about a 15% cut on yards, but the uncut MC was already within -10% to +5% of actuals. Leak-free held-out median signed error (model minus actual, over model) with the cut: passyds -30.4%, rec -9.3%, recyds -12.9%, rushrec -17.2%, rushyds -8.7%. (2) Uncut MC/GR are off by market. MC: passyds -10.5, rec +2.5, recyds +4.3, rushrec -2.4, rushyds +5.0. GR: passyds -9.7, rec -1.4, recyds +2.3, rushrec -4.1, rushyds +2.6. Against ACTUALS, GR's -10% rec/recyds and +9% rushyds lean against the LINES mostly did NOT show up (rec -1.4%, rushyds +2.6%). Most of that lean is model-vs-market disagreement on today's slate, not a model error. The fitted multipliers fix the part that is real. A first fit on only today's leg players gave M of about 1.10-1.17 everywhere. It was rejected as selection-biased: those players were picked for being prominent now, which is look-ahead.
- Fix (2026-11-01): tools/sim_v6.py (v5 untouched). It uses the same simulation core and a leak-free Engine(cutoff). The flat haircut is removed. Each model gets per-market multipliers M = 1 + n/(n+30)*(median(actual/model median) - 1), with M = 1.0 if n < 20. They are fitted on 2026 wk4-7 player-games: 1,096 rows, 110 passyds, 369 rec, 369 recyds, 122 rushrec, 126 rushyds. The universe is pre-cutoff usage thresholds: QB >=20 att, >=4 tgt, >=8 car, >=2 games. The model is fed only pbp before each week. Actuals are nflverse pbp aggregates (the nflverse weekly player_stats definition). No separate weekly file was pulled. Postmortems were not used, because their samples are tiny next to 1,096 rows. Multipliers are in tools/sim_v6_calib.json; the backtest is in tools/sim_v6_backtest.csv. The 'bias' model is now residual-calibrated MC (same multipliers, own RNG stream). Its old flat-haircut role is gone. A heavier-shrink variant (K=60) failed test (a): passyds -3.53%.
- Tests: tools/tests/test_sim_v6.py, written first. RED: ImportError, then the below-line test failed with GR at 60.7%. GREEN: 5/5 OK at SIMV6_TEST_N=4000. (a) Leave-one-week-out held-out median signed error, all within +/-3%: passyds mc/bias -1.82, gr -2.10; rec -1.62/-0.68; recyds +1.54/+0.16; rushrec -0.33/-1.38; rushyds +0.81/-1.41. (b) Share of today's 201 simulated legs (legs_final.json FD lines; the 199-leg manifest set is a subset) with the median below the line: mc 55.7%, bias 54.7%, gr 56.2%. In v5 the figures were bias 85%, MC 52%, GR 57%. (c) Deterministic with a seed; a different seed gives different output. test_run_gate: 30/30 OK.
- Status: FIXED (tests pass). Nov 1 run folders were NOT re-run or edited; they stay on v5 with the avg(MC,GR) edge handling. Future runs: point sim_script at /workspace/nfl-database/tools/sim_v6.py (`python3 tools/sim_v6.py run <legs.json> <out.json>`, or `import sim_v6; sim_v6.Engine().sim(leg)`). Refit weekly with `python3 tools/sim_v6.py fit` after the new pbp is pulled, then re-run `cd tools/tests && python3 -m unittest -v test_sim_v6 test_run_gate`. Once v6 is in use, the edge rule can go back to avg of all 3 models.

