## BUG-2026-11-01-WX (logged 2026-11-01 14:44 ET): Phase 11 weather did not gate overs
- **Symptom:** ATL@TB passed the gate this morning with a 59-63% storm chance and gusts up to 29 mph. Phase 11 was a free-text row; run_gate.py only checked that a weather source existed and was <48 h old.
- **Fix (test-first):** tools/run_gate.py (backup tools/run_gate.py.bak_20261101_1440), with 12 new tests in tools/tests/test_run_gate.py `WeatherTest`.
  - The manifest needs a `weather` block per game (roof, precip_pct, gust_mph, wind_mph, source, pulled_et). It fails closed if the block is missing, the roof is missing, or an open-air game lacks any of the 3 inputs.
  - Weather sources and blocks must be under 6 h old.
  - A game is flagged when its roof is open and precip ≥50%, gusts ≥20 mph, or sustained wind ≥15 mph.
  - In a flagged game, any live passing/receiving OVER (rec, rec yds, pass yds, completions, rush+rec) fails the gate unless it is CUT.
  - The output prints a WEATHER ALERT block with the user's placed legs in the game, from manifest `placed_legs` or a team match in week8/slips/slips_2026-11-01.md.
- **Applied 14:41-14:43 ET:** week8/weather/pull_wx_1440.py (NWS gridpoints) and apply_wx_1442.py (manifest backups *.bak_1442). NE@MIA is FLAGGED (69% / 24.2 mph gusts). No live overs were in that folder.

## BUG-2026-11-01-RBSCRIPT — game-script RB rule (opened & fixed 2026-11-01 ~15:25–15:31 ET)
- Symptom: IND@JAX Tuten O59.5 (JAX -10.5 vs IND 4.49 RB YPC, sustained-wind flag) cut solely by Phase 7 carry share; Tuten ran 104 yds. RB2 Rodriguez was never modeled.
- Fix (TDD; backups tools/run_gate.py.bak_20261101_1525, tools/sim_v6.py.bak_20261101_1525): trigger = fav by 7+ AND opp RB YPC >= 4.4, OR Phase-11 weather flag. sim_v6 `carry_boost` scales carries in all 3 models; `price_game_script` re-prices the lead back and models the RB2; weather games model rushing overs first. run_gate requires a `game_script_rb` block per game (fail closed when weather-flagged or any leg spread <= -7) and waives a Phase-7-only FAIL for a lead-RB rush leg re-priced on the boosted script; every other check still applies.
- Fitted boosts (week8/rbscript/fit_rb_boost.py -> tools/rb_script_boost.json; 2025+2026 REG pbp; K=30 shrink): lead fav x1.001 (n36), lead wx x1.073 (n65), RB2 fav x1.017, RB2 wx x1.110. Favorite status alone barely moves carries.
- Fixture: Tuten re-priced p .727/.726/.717 vs no-vig .577 (edge +14.6, shrunk +7.9); Rodriguez medians 29.9/29.9/29.5. sim_v6 calibration unchanged (boost 1.0 path identical) — no refit.
- Tonight: only NE@MIA triggers (weather); no live legs there. PHI@WSH does not trigger (WSH -5.5, PHI 4.26 YPC, no weather).

## BUG-2026-11-01-RBMISS — Allen/Pollard/Warren misses (fixes A, D, E, F; B and C NOT approved/not built) (2026-11-01 ~15:31–15:39 ET)
- Postmortem: postmortems/RB_MISSES_2026-11-01.md. Backups: tools/run_gate.py.bak_20261101_1540, tools/sim_v6.py.bak_20261101_1540.
- A promotion: sim_v6.promote_rb — RB1 OUT/IR -> RB2 share = own + tau x injured share (games both active); carries target vs RB2's own weighted carries (no double count). Gate: rb_status rb1 OUT/IR/inactive requires rb_promotions[team] (3-model p/median, tau+source) — fail closed.
  Fit (week8/rbmiss/fit_rbmiss.py -> tools/rb_miss_fit.json): tau = 0.392 (n=66 RB1-absent team-games, 90% CI 0.28–0.50). The requested ~75% is NOT supported by pbp; fit used.
- D dog-RB exception (gate): rush-yds over, underdog, all 3 medians > line, (backup out per rb_status OR share >= 70%), line <= main line -> waives only underdog/trailing-script FAILs on phases 6/7/13. Every other check still applies.
- E split re-price: sim_v6.split_reprice prices both backs at lo/mid/hi carry share (last 4 active games; carries-based — Wk8 snap counts unpublished). Gate: split_flag leg needs split_reprice with both backs (fail closed).
- F soft run D: >= 4.4 RB YPC allowed -> fitted YPC boost (`ypc_boost`, all 3 models). Fit on leak-free backtest residuals: 0.948 (n_soft 38, CI 0.57–1.32) -> applied 1.0 (model's existing opp-YPC multiplier already covers it). Gate requires the soft_run_d record. 4.3 -> no boost.
- sim_v6 calibration unchanged (new keys default 1.0).

## 2026-11-01 ~5:00 PM ET: test_explosives.py "no drive match ARI@DAL Q5 5:13"
- Symptom: playlogs/tools/test_explosives.py FAILed on the ARI@DAL OT row (Q5 5:13, Allgeier 11-yd rush).
- Root cause: **not the OT label.** Both the plays file and the row use "Q5". ESPN's play text has a leading space ("[Rush]  T.Allgeier ..."). The plays regex kept that space, while the markdown table cell was stripped, so the 60-character text keys never matched.
- Fix: added play_key(clock, text) to test_explosives.py. It strips text whitespace and the score suffix, and maps OT/OT1 to Q5 as a guard. Both the drive-index side and the row lookup now use it. The main code is behind __name__ so it can be imported. Backup: test_explosives.py.pre_otfix.bak.
- Test first: playlogs/tools/test_explosives_matchkey.py covers the leading-space case and OT vs Q5. It failed against the old file (no play_key; the import ran the old FAIL) and passes now.
- TEN@CIN OT row (Q5 8:32, Higgins 21) matched before and after the fix.
- Result: test_explosives.py PASS, 33 rows. No data rows were edited.
- Note: the Allgeier row is an 11-yard rush, below the new 15+ rush threshold in the defense dissection. It is a legacy-threshold row and was left as is.

