## 2026-11-01 ~22:20 ET — slate_scan missed RB rush-yds candidates (Mike Washington Jr., LV Wk8)
- Cause: RB2 got ryds only on a trigger (weather/favored/starter_out). As an underdog, LV gave Washington only rec/recyds, even though he had 45% and 43% of team carries in Weeks 6-7. In Week 8 he went 25-83.
- Fix (tools/slate_scan.py, backup .pre_rb_rush.bak):
  - Any active RB with >=20% of team carries in either of the team's last 2 games gets ryds (trigger carry_share). This includes RB3+.
  - Passing depth_rb1=<pid> forces a ryds candidate (trigger depth_rb1).
  - Role flip: RB2 out-carried RB1 last game -> swap roles (trigger role_flip).
  - Rule 5 is untouched: non-RB1 rush overs keep rule5_conflict=True.
- Audit Wk3-8 (Wk1-2 can't be scanned; the stand-in line needs 2 prior games): 58 RB ryds candidates were missing (51 carry_share, 7 role_flip). 31 went over the stand-in line. backtests/scan_press/rb_rush_missing_wk3_8.csv

## 2026-11-01 ~22:45 ET — Source audit (SOURCE_AUDIT_2026-11-01.md): three pipeline bugs
**SA-1 wind None-as-0 (fixed).** tools/scan_data.py and backtests/wk8_proposals/harness.py set wx with `g.wind.fillna(0) >= 15`. Root cause: nflverse `wind` is NaN in 31 of 75 2026 outdoor games, but the `weather` string still has "Wind: NE 13 mph". So missing wind silently read as calm. Fix: new `scan_data._wind_mph()` uses the numeric value, else parses the string ("Calm" = 0); unknown stays NaN. Test: tools/tests/test_wind_parse.py. Impact Wk1-8: one game crossed 15 mph (2026_06_HOU_JAX, 16 mph), and it was already flagged for rain, so no wx flag changed. Backups: *.pre_wind.bak.
**SA-2 WX8 missed NE@MIA (fixed).** scan_data.WX8 only had ATL@TB, but phase15_4pm flagged NE@MIA (NWS PoP 53-69%, open air), which meets the 50%+ rain rule. Added it. Test is in test_wind_parse.py. Suites slate_scan, press_wire, rbmiss_sim, wind_parse and odds_pregame are all OK.
**SA-3 in-play odds mixed into pregame pulls (helper landed; pull_odds patch pending).** runs/2026-11-01_shared_src/pull_odds.py has no kickoff check. The Odds API keeps returning live markets, so odds_i1435 has 5055/10206 rows, odds_b1442 5044, odds_g1529 3517 and odds_i1850 1062/2188 rows quoted after kickoff. Example: Stafford pass yds DK 168.5 vs Pinnacle 248.5. The 14:35, 15:29 and 18:51 re-pulls were used only for games not yet started (4 PM and SNF), so no placed leg was found priced off a live line. Any later reuse of those files for line history is contaminated. New tools/odds_pregame.py (pregame_events, flag_inplay; unknown kickoff = None, never pregame). Tests: tools/tests/test_odds_pregame.py. Patch: audits/source_audit_patches/pull_odds_pregame.patch.md.
